      ],
      "source": "https://eastlandtexas.gov/history",
      "category": "economy",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "In 1928 the current courthouse was built, and a local lizard named 'Old Rip' gained national fame before dying in 1929 and being displayed in the courthouse.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        15,
        16,
        17
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
